{
 "_help": [
  "Rules that turn OpenStreetMap tags into tqt layers (the working file of tMC). Edited by hand; the program does not read the \"examples\" array.",
  "The rules are checked from top to bottom; an object goes into the layer of the FIRST matching rule (unless \"continue\": true is set).",
  "from  : the OSM driver layer — multipolygons (buildings, plots, sites), lines (roads, rails), points (points).",
  "layer : the tqt layer suffix: bldpol, vegpol, vgbpol, rdslin, rrslin, csrpol, rdcpol, blkpol, hdrpol, hdrlin; \"-\" — drop the object (no further rules are checked).",
  "as    : polygon (a closed line -> a polygon), line (a polygon boundary -> a line), square:N (a point -> a square with a side of N meters), crosswalk:N (a crossing node -> a line of N meters across the nearest motor road).",
  "pass  : 1 (default) — by tags; 2 — a \"guess\" for buildings not recognized on the 1st pass: they see the nb:* tags about the neighbors.",
  "when  : conditions on tags (all at once). \"v\" — equals; \"*\" — the tag exists; \"-\" or null — no tag; \"!v\" — the tag exists and is not equal to v;",
  "        [\"a\",\"b\"] — one of; [\"!a\",\"!b\"] — the tag exists and is not from the list; \"~regex\"; numbers \">=4\", \"<250\" (the first number from the tag value).",
  "        Service tags: poi:<tag> — tags of the points inside the building outline; area:<tag> — tags of the enclosing plots (without building);",
  "        _area — the outline area, m2; _perim — the perimeter, m; nb:code / nb:share / nb:n / nb:rel / nb:dist — neighbors (pass 2 only).",
  "fields: the tqt layer fields (CODE, REL, MAT ...). The value: text with substitutions {tag}, {tag1,tag2} (the first non-empty),",
  "        {tag|num}, {tag|int}, {tag|num*3}, {osm_id}; alternatives through || (the first non-empty). REL=\"auto\": height -> building:levels by the",
  "        floor recalculation formulas (by CODE and the outline shape) -> heights.csv by CODE -> 6 m.",
  "Address: the fields TYSTR (street type), STREET (name) and NUMBR (house number) for bldpol and the street name for rdslin are filled IN BY THEMSELVES from addr:street/addr:place/addr:full/addr:housenumber and name",
  "        (osm/tmcaddress.cpp): \"улица Ленина\" -> TYSTR=улица, STREET=Ленина; \"12к1\" -> 12К.1. If a rule sets these fields explicitly, its value is taken.",
  "The tags from the conditions and templates automatically become columns of the temporary osmconf.ini, the others are read from other_tags.",
  "db:code / db:rel / db:floor — the enhancer data (tmc_buildings.dat): the type, height and floor count of the nearest point; a fallback if OSM did not determine it.",
  "greenery: completing the vegetation for OSM (yards between houses, forced taiga in the private sector, forests up to the forest_share of the area, parks no fewer than parks_per_km2 per km²; the grid step cell_m, m). enabled=false turns it off.",
  "greenery.wild_forests: on very big empty plots (from wild_min_area_m2 m² after the margins) forests for bandit camps and bases are added (no more than wild_max_count); the margin from buildings wild_building_m, from block development wild_block_m, m — there are none between high-rises."
 ],
 "neighbors": {
  "radius_m": 60,
  "ignore_codes": [
   "44000000"
  ]
 },
 "rules": [
  {
   "note": "Not buildings in the sense of the model: canopies, roofs, bridges, ruins, tents",
   "from": "multipolygons",
   "layer": "-",
   "when": {
    "building": [
     "roof",
     "ruins",
     "bridge",
     "tent",
     "carport",
     "no"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "note": "WATER: area rivers (natural=water + water=river/oxbow/stream, waterway=riverbank) — hdrpol 31410000",
   "from": "multipolygons",
   "layer": "hdrpol",
   "when": {
    "building": "-",
    "natural": "water",
    "water": ["river", "oxbow", "stream", "stream_pool"]
   },
   "fields": { "CODE": "31410000" }
  },
